diff --git a/docs/configurable-contract.md b/docs/configurable-contract.md
index ad5ec2d7..9bd4d2c2 100644
--- a/docs/configurable-contract.md
+++ b/docs/configurable-contract.md
@@ -60,6 +60,21 @@ The derived digest includes every final action and its provenance. Catalog
 version changes require explicit revalidation, so a saved recipe cannot
 silently acquire a newly cataloged operation.
 
+Catalog 1 remains the default and keeps its existing operation set. Explicit
+`catalog = 2` selects the configured-operation extension: `lstat`, `readv`,
+`pipe`, `nanosleep`, `link`, `sched_getaffinity`, `clock_getres`, `faccessat`,
+`renameat2` and `execveat`. The legacy `configured-balanced-v2` profile selects
+the same catalog. Catalog 1 wildcards never acquire these operations; unknown
+catalog versions fail validation. The selected version participates in the
+digest, and instance inspection and diff report the selected operation set.
+
+Catalog selection compiles authority, not an implementation of these calls.
+The execution backend still determines which operations it supports and must
+apply its own argument and resource checks. This extension does not implement
+configured storage, clocks, networking or process supervision, and does not
+expand native policy. Its fixture names identify the intended owning features;
+those runtime contributions remain separate from catalog versioning.
+
 Gate 10 `[contract]` profiles and templates remain accepted internally for
 migration and regression comparison, but they cannot be mixed with
 `[userspace.contract]`. New saved examples use the self-contained form. Copy a
